          "name": "Get tenant info",
          "request": {
            "name": "Get tenant info",
            "description": {
              "content": "[operation: tenant-get]\n\n\n\nREAD-ONLY\n\n\n\nFetches top-level config and metadata for the authenticated org — the tenant is inferred from the API key, so there are no inputs. Use it to learn the org's subdomain and cluster, which other calls fold into URLs and identifiers.\n\n→\n\n    {tenantData: {tenantId, cluster, subdomain}, tenantType: \"Personal\"|\"Organization\", email (Personal only), domains: [...] (Organization only)}\n\n  Note: tenantId is at tenantData.tenantId (not top-level); subdomain is at tenantData.subdomain\n\nsee: meeting-activity/crm-activity (use tenantData.subdomain for URL construction)",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
